<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ogunmola</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1867</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ogunmola was a war chief of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibadan">Ibadan</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> military state, who rose through success in battle to hold the title of Bashorun in the 1860s. He led Ibadan's campaigns that extended its power over the Ijesha and Ekiti towns and fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ijaye">Ijaye</a> War of 1860-1862. He is remembered as one of the great generals of 19th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yorubaland">Yorubaland</a>.</p></div>
